On 10 April three hundred thousand follow the coffins. Our banners say "Murdered by French and German capital". The union banners say "Murdered".

@strike
subtitle: The pits stop and the strike may spread. The French bring up armoured cars.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0 or ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
RG.startStrike('ruhr');
RG.spreadStrike('ruhr');
RG.district('ruhr', {repression: 8, guards: 1});
Q.e23_krupp = 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

For three days the strike holds from Duisburg to Dortmund. Then the strike pay runs out, and the French bring up armoured cars.

@french
subtitle: The nationalists are outraged. Some French conscripts listen.
view-if: e23_ruhr_line = 1 or e23_ruhr_line = 2
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 4);
Q.e23_krupp = 3;
Q.world_revolution += 4;
Q.army_loyalty -= 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

A delegate of the French party speaks at the graveside in bad German, and is arrested by his own army at the cemetery gate. A week later two French soldiers in Gelsenkirchen hand their rifles to the hundreds.
